A prepended stub dir is an allowlist implemented as a blocklist: it
intercepts the tools it remembered to fake and passes everything else
through to the real binary, silently, because the un-faked tool works.

bindir_with_fakes(gh=False) placed no fake gh, but /usr/bin/gh stayed
reachable, so scripts/contribute:240's `command -v gh` probe succeeded
and the class named TestGitHubFallbackWhenGhAbsent ran with gh present --
the real binary calling api.github.com/graphql and failing on HTTP 401.
It passed on CI only because those runners have no gh: a green that
measured the runner image rather than the code.

No prepend-side trick fixes it. A shim satisfies `command -v`; a
directory or dangling symlink named gh is skipped and the lookup
continues; and gh sits in /usr/bin beside git, sed and awk, so filtering
its directory would take the script's real dependencies with it. The
harness now builds a shadow dir -- one symlink per executable on the
inherited PATH, minus gh, built once per process (~400ms) -- and runs
scripts with the fake bindir followed by that shadow.

An env seam in scripts/contribute was the alternative and was rejected:
it puts a test-only branch in production code, and that file is
governance. The harness-only fix needs neither.

Credential exposure closed too: the scrub list popped FORGEJO_TOKEN,
SELFHOSTED_FORGEJO_TOKEN and HG_GITHUB_TOKEN -- none of which gh reads --
while omitting GH_TOKEN, GITHUB_TOKEN and GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN, which it
does. All were unset where this was found, so the observed failure was an
unauthenticated 401; on a box with `gh auth login` the same test would
have driven an authenticated client.

Scope corrected downward from the filing: there is exactly ONE
`command -v gh` probe in scripts/, ONE failing test, and the fixture
upstream is the placeholder github.com/up/r, so an authenticated run
would have produced an API error, not a real PR. The filed "19 call
sites" counted uses of the helper, not exposure.

Also fixed, because this change could not otherwise be verified in CI:
smart-test now always runs a test file you edited, root tests included.
The changed-test pattern covered only packages/*/tests/, AND the check
sat inside the TDD fallback that fires only when nothing else was
selected -- so an edited root test alongside any mapped source was
silently dropped. Now computed once and unioned unconditionally.
scripts/smart-test had no tests at all; tests/test_smart_test.py starts
that coverage by extracting the live regex from the script rather than
restating it.

The WI-bisar ratchet caught this change's own new harness test one commit
after shipping; recorded in KNOWN_UNREACHABLE with reasoning, since it
covers a test helper -- a category of exactly one.

Full root suite: 1427 passed.

